  {
   "id": "S05",
   "act": "ACT3",
   "title": "TSMC, ASML, memory, packaging",
   "lead_in": 0.0,
   "tail": 0.4,
   "vo": [
    {
     "id": "L040",
     "text": "Manufacturing goes to Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company, or TSMC.",
     "pause": 0.3
    },
    {
     "id": "L041",
     "text": "By one industry estimate, it took nearly three-quarters of all contract chipmaking revenue in the second quarter of 2026.",
     "say": "By one industry estimate, it took nearly three-quarters of all contract chipmaking revenue in the second quarter of twenty twenty-six.",
     "pause": 0.3
    },
    {
     "id": "L042",
     "text": "High-performance computing now makes up about two-thirds of its sales. And it has told investors it plans to spend up to sixty-four billion dollars on new capacity this year.",
     "pause": 0.5
    },
    {
     "id": "L043",
     "text": "TSMC, in turn, relies on a single Dutch company.",
     "pause": 0.3
    },
    {
     "id": "L044",
     "text": "ASML is the world's only maker of the extreme ultraviolet lithography machines used to print the most advanced chips.",
     "pause": 0.3
    },
    {
     "id": "L045",
     "text": "The newest models are reported to cost hundreds of millions of dollars each.",
     "pause": 0.5
    },
    {
     "id": "L046",
     "text": "Then there is memory. SK hynix makes the high-bandwidth memory stacked beside each AI processor. In its latest quarter, it reported an operating margin of around eighty percent.",
     "pause": 0.4
    },
    {
     "id": "L047",
     "text": "And the finished pieces must be bonded together, in a process called advanced packaging. Another bottleneck, and another place TSMC is pouring money.",
     "pause": 0.6
    }
   ],
