  {
   "id": "S07",
   "act": "ACT4",
   "title": "The data centre economy",
   "lead_in": 0.4,
   "tail": 0.3,
   "vo": [
    {
     "id": "L060",
     "text": "A chip is only useful inside a building that can power it and cool it.",
     "pause": 0.35
    },
    {
     "id": "L061",
     "text": "And an AI data centre is not a warehouse of computers. It is an industrial machine.",
     "pause": 0.45
    },
    {
     "id": "L062",
     "text": "Nvidia's latest rack-scale systems are specified at around one hundred and twenty kilowatts per rack. That's many times what a typical server rack was built for.",
     "pause": 0.3
    },
    {
     "id": "L063",
     "text": "Air can no longer carry that much heat away. So liquid is piped straight to the chips.",
     "pause": 0.5
    }
   ],
   "shots": [
    {
     "asset": "DC-010",
     "in": 122,
     "need": "Long aisle of supercomputer racks",
     "dim": 0.2
    },
    {
     "asset": "DC-010",
     "in": 31,
