   "id": "S10",
   "act": "ACT5",
   "title": "Generation, grid, transformers",
   "lead_in": 0.0,
   "tail": 0.4,
   "vo": [
    {
     "id": "L090",
     "text": "First, the power has to be generated. Big Tech is now signing deals to restart nuclear reactors.",
     "pause": 0.3
    },
    {
     "id": "L091",
     "text": "Microsoft agreed to buy the output of Three Mile Island's Unit One for twenty years, if it comes back online.",
     "pause": 0.4
    },
    {
     "id": "L092",
     "text": "Gas turbines are in such demand that GE Vernova's gas backlog and reserved production slots have reached one hundred and twenty-two gigawatts.",
     "pause": 0.5
    },
    {
     "id": "L093",
     "text": "Then the power has to be delivered. And here, the bottleneck is physical.",
     "pause": 0.4
    },
    {
     "id": "L094",
     "text": "Berkeley Lab found that the typical American power project built in 2025 waited around five years to connect to the grid.",
     "say": "Berkeley Lab found that the typical American power project built in twenty twenty-five waited around five years to connect to the grid.",
     "pause": 0.4
    },
    {
     "id": "L095",
     "text": "And every connection needs transformers. A large power transformer can weigh hundreds of tonnes, and the wait for one is commonly two years or more. For the largest units, up to four.",
     "pause": 0.3
    },
    {
     "id": "L096",
     "text": "Prices have climbed too: up sixty to eighty percent since 2020, according to Wood Mackenzie.",
